   if (!b) {
       return NULL;
   }
   ```
   Memory is allocated based on the calculated remaining buffer size. This is appropriate as it allocates exactly the amount of memory needed.

3. **Reading Data**:
   ```c
   int available = r_buf_read_at (buf, off, b, size);
   if (available != size) {
       eprintf ("Warning: r_buf_read_at failed\n");
       return NULL;
   }
